  "narrative": "<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Short impact summary</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Character Constellations shows early signs of reach and use: it has been downloaded 1,663 times through OAPEN, has been discussed in public-facing channels indexed by Crossref, and is supported by funding from KU Leuven, the Graduate School for the Humanities of Radboud University, and the J. E. Jurriaanse Stichting. The record is still thin on citation uptake, but the available evidence indicates that the book is already being accessed and circulated.</p>\n<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Full narrative</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Roel Smeets\u2019s Character Constellations brings data-driven methods to the study of fiction, using a corpus of 170 contemporary Dutch-language novels to examine how characters are represented across gender, race, ethnicity, class, age, sexuality, and related identity categories. Its framing sits at the intersection of literary study, sociology, network analysis, and gender studies, and the publication was produced with support from KU Leuven, the Graduate School for the Humanities of Radboud University, and the J. E. Jurriaanse Stichting.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">The clearest impact signal in the record is use: the book has registered 1,663 OAPEN downloads, suggesting that it is being actively consulted rather than remaining a purely archival publication. The monthly pattern shows sustained access over time, which is consistent with an audience engaging with the book as a research resource.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Public discourse is present but modest. Crossref-indexed attention records two mentions, indicating that the book has entered some scholarly or public-facing conversation, though the evidence does not yet show a broad surrounding media footprint. In the citation record, OpenAlex currently reports no citations, so scholarly uptake has not yet accumulated in that channel.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">The book\u2019s open-access availability likely supports its reach. OpenAIRE identifies it as hybrid open access and lists multiple open instances, including a hosted PDF, which lowers barriers for readers and may help explain the observed download activity. Overall, Character Constellations appears to be an accessible and methodologically distinctive scholarly book whose immediate footprint is stronger in readership and circulation than in citation-based impact.</p>",
